---
// Public privacy policy for the Play Store listings. Deliberately indexable
// (noindex={false}) and covers every game, so one URL serves all listings.
import MinimalLayout from "../layout/MinimalLayout.astro";

const updated = "October 1, 2026";
const contactEmail = "farooqinfocus@gmail.com";
---

<MinimalLayout title="Privacy Policy — Farooq Zahid" noindex={false}>
  <p class="not-prose mb-8 text-sm">
    <a class="text-blue-600 underline" href="/">← mfarooqzahid.github.io</a>
  </p>

  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated: {updated}</em></p>

  <p>
    This Privacy Policy describes how Farooq Zahid ("we", "us") handles
    information when you use our mobile games <strong>Emoji Mashup</strong> and
    <strong>Cat Stack</strong> (each, "the App"). It applies to the Android
    versions of both Apps.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

  <h3>Data stored locally on your device</h3>
  <p>
    Both Apps are designed to work fully offline. The following is saved locally
    on your device only, and is <strong>not</strong> transmitted to us:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Emoji Mashup:</strong> game progress and level completion,
      discovered creations and ingredients, star ratings earned per level, and
      app settings and preferences.</li>
    <li><strong>Cat Stack:</strong> game progress and levels reached, star
      ratings earned per level, and app settings and preferences (sound, music,
      crate speed).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not collect, store, or have access to this data ourselves.</p>

  <h3>Advertising data</h3>
  <p>
    The Apps display ads through <strong>Google AdMob</strong>. Emoji Mashup
    shows rewarded video ads (used to unlock hints) and interstitial ads; Cat
    Stack shows interstitial ads between levels. AdMob may collect certain
    information automatically to serve and measure ads, including:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Device identifiers (such as the Advertising ID)</li>
    <li>IP address and general location</li>
    <li>App usage data related to ad interactions</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This data is collected and processed by Google in accordance with the
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
      >Google Privacy Policy</a
    >
    and
    <a
      href="https://support.google.com/admob/answer/6128543"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noreferrer">Google's AdMob data collection practices</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h3>Purchases</h3>
  <p>
    Each App offers a single optional purchase, <strong>Remove Ads</strong>,
    processed by <strong>Google Play Billing</strong>. We do not receive or store
    your payment details; Google handles that information under its own terms
    and privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
  <p>
    Since we do not collect personal data ourselves, we do not use, sell, or
    share any personal information. Locally stored game data is used solely to
    let you resume your progress on your own device.
  </p>
  <p>Ad-related data collected by Google AdMob is used to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Serve ads</li>
    <li>Measure ad performance</li>
    <li>Prevent fraud and abuse</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    The Apps are designed with children in mind and follow applicable children's
    privacy laws, including the U.S. Children's Online Privacy Protection Act
    (COPPA) and the GDPR provisions for children. We do not knowingly collect
    personal information from children.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ad serving is handled through Google AdMob with child-directed treatment:
    every ad request is made with the age treatment set to child and a maximum
    ad content rating of "G" (general audiences). As a result, ads are requested
    in a child-appropriate, non-personalized way, and the Android advertising
    identifier is not used to personalize ads for these Apps.
  </p>
  <p>
    Parents and guardians with questions about ads shown to children should
    review Google's policies linked above, or contact us using the details in
    Section 8.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Data Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We do not share, sell, or rent any personal data, because we do not collect
    any ourselves. Any data shared with third parties (such as Google AdMob and
    Google Play Billing) is limited to what is described in Section 1 and is
    governed by that third party's own privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Locally stored data (progress, discoveries, stars, settings) remains on your
    device until you uninstall an App or clear its data through your device
    settings. We have no ability to access or delete this data remotely, as we
    never receive it.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Third-Party Services</h2>
  <p>The Apps use the following third-party services:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google AdMob</strong> — for displaying ads. See
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
        >Google's Privacy Policy</a
      >.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Play Billing</strong> — for the optional Remove Ads
      purchase. See
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
        >Google's Privacy Policy</a
      >.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be
    reflected by updating the "Last updated" date at the top of this page.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Contact Us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at:
    <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <hr />

  <p>
    <em
      >This policy applies to the Android versions of Emoji Mashup (package:
      <code>com.farooq.emojimashup</code>) and Cat Stack (package:
      <code>com.farooq.catstack</code>).</em
    >
  </p>
</MinimalLayout>
